                "text": "**Defining the Rule**\n\nOkay, I've got a grasp of the verifier rule now. It's essentially identifying the \"odd one out\" in a sequence of visually similar elements, in this case, a row of panels. The key is that all panels share a common shape and size, but one panel will have a unique shape. My focus is now on the criteria for what makes that shape \"odd\".\n\n\n**Clarifying the Criteria**\n\nI've refined the criteria for the \"odd\" panel. It's the one with a unique pattern of filled cells; number, size, color, or layout don't matter. Square panels must be side x side, with at least 3 panels in a row or column. All but one share the exact cell pattern. Now, I have four clean examples to build on.\n\n\n",
